    description: "Surfaced by WI-tolap (route-parity re-measure). When a route surfaces via a synthesized route-marker symbol (id shape '<lang>:<file>:<span>:<METHOD> <path>:route', e.g. 'java:Ctrl.java:5-6:GET /users:route', 'go:main.go:8-8:ANY /users:route', 'javascript:app.js:3-3:GET /users:route'), that symbol violates THREE validators simultaneously in the emitted validation_report: (1) id_format WARNING x2 — the id's kind-slot 'route' does not match Symbol.kind 'function' (round-trip violation) AND 'route' is not a registered symbol-kind (symbol_kinds.all_symbol_kind_names()); (2) cross_field ERROR — empty origin_run_id, breaking node->AnalysisRun referential integrity; (3) axis_conformance ERROR — Symbol.origin contains an invalid element. Reproduced live 2026-07-02 on packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/fixtures/route-parity/{go,javascript,java} via run_behavior_map. PRE-EXISTING and language-agnostic: go and javascript emit the identical triple TODAY (independent of WI-tolap, which only made java join them). python/rust route via concept=route on the function itself and synthesize NO marker, so they do not exhibit it — the 3-mechanism surfacing inconsistency the WI-tosul re-measure documented. Producer is the route-marker synthesis path (http linker / route materialization). Structural fix likely: mint the marker via make_symbol_id with a REGISTERED kind (register 'route' per ADR-0027 or fold to a canonical kind), populate origin_run_id, set a conformant Symbol.origin. Related (do NOT fold): WI-mosil (done — general empty origin_run_id sweep; route-marker synthesizer is an uncovered producer or regression), INV-popop (route stable_id collisions), INV-nubub (route-symbol slice collision). Behavioral close-check: route-parity fixtures' validation_report shows 0 route-marker id_format/cross_field/axis_conformance violations across go/js/java."  # ac78
    fields: {}  # ac78
