  message: "Done via PR #382 (dev 104a2bb491 fix + c22d9c11de test-gate). Behavioral close-check (this item's filed repro) re-run on merged dev: run_behavior_map on fixtures/route-parity/{go,javascript,java} shows 0 route-marker id_format/cross_field/axis_conformance violations across all three. Markers now build the id via make_symbol_id kind=function (id-slot round-trips Symbol.kind=function), carry a non-empty origin_run_id joining a real AnalysisRun, and name a registered origin pass-id (go=[go]; js/java=[route-materializer]). Fix: framework_patterns materializers + the go route pass build the id with kind=function; cli.run_behavior_map mints a real AnalysisRun per materialization pass (route-materializer / django-cbv-method-expander, registered in catalog._BUILTIN_PIPELINE_PASS_IDS + pass_metadata.GAP_PASSES) and threads execution_id into origin_run_id. No new symbol-kind axis: nothing consumes the id kind-slot (all six route consumers key on meta.framework_role). Filed premise that go and js emit the identical triple was REFUTED on re-measure: go already stamped origin/origin_run_id (only the advisory id-slot warning), so the two errors were js/java-materializer-only. Scope = route-parity trio; the remaining route producers (js_ts/py.py-direct, ruby/php/elixir/swift/scala, grpc, go route_mount, annotation_convention) still carry the id-slot fossil, filed as WI-zugob. No awaits_bakeoff_validation: provenance/id-form fix, the id-slot is unconsumed, no bakeoff-metric claim."  # 9679
